There are several other ways to make unholy water which will have less 
effect on your intrinsics and alignment:

- read a blessed scroll of remove curse with lots of individually #named 
uncursed potions of water in your inventory - chances are good one will end 
up cursed.

- #dip uncursed potions of water into a fountain - one of the effects is 
cursing the dipped item (1/30)

- (q)aff from a fountain with lots of individually #named uncursed potions 
of water in your inventory - one of the effects is cursing your inventory 
(1/30 chance of effect, 1/5 chance per item of a curse - #dipping is 
better)

- Get cursed by a monster that can do this (e.g. arch-lich).

- wish for it

Remember that other things could get cursed too if you make use of one of 
the inventory techniques - you'll want to drop or stash most of your gear 
beforehand (a cursed sack works just as well as an uncursed one).

But I think that the OP wants to curse ?oGD to detect portals. This isn't 
the best way to do it - you want to read non-cursed ?oGD while confused. A 
cursed scroll detects traps (including portals) as gold, which disappears 
when it's in LoS. A confused scroll detects them as the correct trap, and 
is permanent. If you don't like the idea of being stunned on the elemental 
plains (never bothered me except on Air, where I allow myself to get 
swallowed by a vortex first) take along some potions of booze or confusion. 
The booze must not be blessed.

A crystal ball is also useful for detecting portals, although rather heavy 
- but it's useful to remember if you happen to have an artifact example.


